# Run outputs: CSV logs, camera recordings, ROS logs.
# Each machine writes into its own workspace (ws_jetson/runs/, ws_rpi/runs/,
# ws_base/runs/), so match a `runs/` directory at any depth rather than only
# the old shared top-level one. Unanchored so it covers every workspace.
# Note this deliberately also covers *.avi -- camera_recorder_node writes
# ~25 GB/hour, which must never be a candidate for `git add -A`.
runs/

# Build artifacts
build/
install/
log/
*.egg-info/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Temporary files
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Production main policy: keep local POC/tracing outputs untracked
ws_base/tools/

# D415 capture utility output (Windows laptop tool, not workspace-scoped)
tools/videocapture/

# ---- Rust rewrite (branch `rs`) ----
target/
# Cargo.lock is committed deliberately, in all three places it exists (root
# workspace + firmware/chassis + firmware/sensors, which are separate
# workspaces): this is an application/firmware project, not a published
# library, and reproducible builds matter more than floating to the latest
# compatible dependency. See firmware/chassis/Cargo.toml's own note on the
# yanked `bisync` crate for exactly the failure mode a committed lockfile
# prevents on a fresh clone.
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code personal settings override (not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json
